{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7439702","formula":"C₃₆H₂₀N₂O₄","hill":"C36H20N2O4","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":36.0,"H":20.0,"N":2.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"Scytonemin"},"descriptions":{"en":"Scytonemin is a secondary metabolite and an extracellular matrix (sheath) pigment synthesized by many strains of cyanobacteria, including Nostoc, Scytonema, Calothrix, Lyngbya, Rivularia, Chlorogloeopsis, and Hyella. Scytonemin-synthesizing cyanobacteria often inhabit highly insolated terrestrial, freshwater and coastal environments such as deserts, semideserts, rocks, cliffs, marine intertidal flats, and hot springs. The pigment was originally discovered in 1849 by Swiss botanist Carl Nägeli, although the structure remained unsolved until 1993."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":135473381,"mass":544.6,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C2N=C\\3C(=C(C(=O)/C3=C/C4=CC=C(C=C4)O)C5=C6C(=NC7=CC=CC=C67)/C(=C\\C8=CC=C(C=C8)O)/C5=O)C2=C1","inchikey":"CGZKSPLDUIRCIO-RPCRKUJJSA-N","iupac":"(3E)-3-[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methylidene]-1-[(3E)-3-[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methylidene]-2-oxocyclopenta[b]indol-1-yl]cyclopenta[b]indol-2-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"135473381","atoms":62,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.207,"y":-3.345,"z":2.586,"el":"C"},{"x":2.591,"y":-3.567,"z":2.719,"el":"C"},{"x":3.518,"y":-2.713,"z":2.112,"el":"C"},{"x":3.038,"y":-1.646,"z":1.377,"el":"C"},{"x":3.832,"y":-0.678,"z":0.697,"el":"N"},{"x":2.97,"y":0.119,"z":0.159,"el":"C"},{"x":1.564,"y":-0.258,"z":0.423,"el":"C"},{"x":0.71,"y":0.586,"z":-0.161,"el":"C"},{"x":1.498,"y":1.62,"z":-0.897,"el":"C"},{"x":1.038,"y":2.501,"z":-1.598,"el":"O"},{"x":2.936,"y":1.322,"z":-0.665,"el":"C"},{"x":3.922,"y":2.061,"z":-1.184,"el":"C"},{"x":5.361,"y":1.831,"z":-1.025,"el":"C"},{"x":6.173,"y":1